          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2><strong>H. Goutorbe: A Family Tradition</strong></h2><h3><strong>Introduction</strong></h3><p>H. Goutorbe is a respected, family-owned Champagne house based in the village of Aÿ in the Montagne de Reims, France. The estate was founded in the early 20th century by Emile Goutorbe and is now managed by his descendants, who continue the family’s long-standing dedication to crafting exceptional Champagne.</p><h3><strong>Location and Terroir</strong></h3><p>The village of Aÿ is one of Champagne’s most celebrated Grand Cru sites, known for its south-facing slopes and chalky soils that provide ideal growing conditions for Pinot Noir. The Goutorbe family owns vineyards primarily in Aÿ, but also in other prestigious crus across the Montagne de Reims. This diversity allows them to produce Champagnes that express both the power of Pinot Noir and the elegance of Chardonnay.</p><h3><strong>Champagnes Offered</strong></h3><h4><strong>Non-Vintage Champagnes</strong></h4><p>H. Goutorbe’s non-vintage Champagnes are carefully blended from Pinot Noir, Chardonnay, and Pinot Meunier grown on the family’s estate. These wines are aged for at least three years on the lees, developing depth, balance, and a signature richness that reflects the character of Aÿ.</p><h4><strong>Vintage Champagnes</strong></h4><p>Produced only in outstanding years, H. Goutorbe’s vintage Champagnes showcase the distinct qualities of each harvest. Aged for a minimum of five years on the lees, these wines display elegance, structure, and remarkable aging potential.</p><h4><strong>Prestige Cuvées</strong></h4><p>At the top of the range are the Prestige Cuvées, crafted from the finest parcels of the family’s oldest vines. These Champagnes are aged for a minimum of seven years, resulting in wines of exceptional finesse, complexity, and longevity — true expressions of the Goutorbe family’s expertise.</p><h3><strong>Winemaking Techniques</strong></h3><p>H. Goutorbe is known for its commitment to traditional methods and meticulous craftsmanship. As both growers and producers, the family controls every stage of production, from vineyard management to bottling. Their approach emphasizes purity of fruit, precise blending, and patient aging to achieve consistent excellence.</p><h3><strong>Conclusion</strong></h3><p>H. Goutorbe embodies the values of a true grower-producer: authenticity, tradition, and dedication to quality. With deep roots in Aÿ and generations of experience, the family continues to craft Champagnes that are both expressive of their terroir and emblematic of the region’s finest traditions.</p>",
